d":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Assignments/Projects","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"Nkk286FSmZ"}],"key":"AGqJ9OEXAD"},{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"6/7","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"otxrJdRuNB"}],"key":"TIiaFibYHa"}],"key":"yr9OcIyDpa"}],"key":"mDmBFxj1Fs"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I found the course was structured well to lead developers into the Android developer tools smoothly. Our first\nproject was implementing a layout using XML, which was a good introduction to the Android Studio IDE. We then\nmoved on to implementing a simple app that used a RecyclerView to display a list of items. Later projects involved\nusing various Android APIs to implement more complex apps and Android features. We implemented app features using\nthe Model-View-ViewModel (MVVM) design pattern, which is a common design pattern for Android apps.","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"qcghchiFaD"}],"key":"oOGpAQIMaP"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The final project was a group project where we implemented a travel planning app. We used the Google Maps API to\nenable saved locations and maps viewing for the users. The main selling point of this app is a feature that allows\nthe user to save a list of locations and then generate a route that visits all the locations in the order that\nis optimized automatically using an optimization algorithm given the user’s preferences.\nYou can read more about my experience with this project in\nmy ","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"jio5rEDuku"},{"type":"link","url":"/city-explorer-app","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Android Development - City Explorer App","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"GIDQq9Z2rz"}],"urlSource":"../android_development/city-explorer-app.md","dataUrl":"/city-explorer-app.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"LHwrBIeFJw"},{"type":"text","value":" page.","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"gliPAEiarP"}],"key":"nEKLqbco4E"}],"key":"QrL7Qm6Vw3"}],"key":"naEsMr9WSp"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Course Reviews","short_title":"Course Reviews","url":"/overview-course-reviews","group":"iOS App Development"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}